# Spec-Driven Development

Every feature uses its own branch and `specs/` directory. Requirements and code stay synchronized.

## Feature Layout

```
specs/<NNN-feature-name>/
├── spec.md    # Requirements (what)
├── plan.md    # Architecture (how)
└── tasks.md   # Implementation steps (when)
```

Branch name MUST match directory: `001-ticket-crud` → `specs/001-ticket-crud/`.

## Workflow Rules

1. **Record prompts** — append every user prompt to `docs/prompt-history.md` (redact secrets)
2. **Spec first** — create/update `spec.md` before writing code
3. **Commit artifacts** — every change to spec/plan/tasks/prompt-history gets its own Git commit
4. **Propagate changes** — requirement change → update spec → plan → tasks → code
5. **One feature per branch** — never mix spec artifacts from different features
6. **Analyze before implement** — run `/speckit.analyze` after plan and tasks

## Prompt History Entry

Append to `docs/prompt-history.md`:

```
## <timestamp>
**Branch**: <branch>  **Feature**: <specs/NNN-name/ or —>  **Agent**: cursor
**Prompt**: > verbatim user message
**Outcome**: files changed / decisions made
```

## Pull Requests

PRs MUST include the feature's `spec.md`, `plan.md`, `tasks.md`, code, and tests.
PR description MUST link to `specs/<feature>/` and list acceptance criteria addressed.

## Active Feature Detection

Spec Kit resolves the active feature from Git branch name or `SPECIFY_FEATURE` env var.
Always work on the matching feature branch when editing spec artifacts.
